{
  "requirement": "Validation MUST read the mdBook source directory from `[book].src` in `book.toml`, using `src` when the setting is absent. It MUST report an unreadable or malformed book configuration and reject an empty, absolute, or parent-traversing source path.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "No gaps found. Each obligation in `requirements.ci.book_source` is carried out by `book_source_dir` (src/evidence.rs 358–412). That function carries an {impl} reference to the requirement, and a test asserts the outcome of each obligation.\n\nObligations and their code:\n- **Read the source directory from `[book].src` in `book.toml`.** `book_source_dir` reads and parses `book.toml`, accepts `book` as a table or inline table, reads `src` as a string, and returns `root.join(relative)`.\n- **Use `src` when the setting is absent.** The `None => \"src\"` arm covers a missing `src` key. A missing `[book]` table or an empty file gives `table = None`, which also falls through to `src`.\n- **Report an unreadable book configuration.** A failed `fs::read_to_string` pushes \"book.toml: cannot read book configuration: …\".\n- **Report a malformed book configuration.** A TOML parse error pushes \"invalid TOML\". A non-table `book` pushes \"book must be a table\". A non-string `book.src` pushes \"book.src must be a string\".\n- **Reject an empty source path.** `source.is_empty()` pushes \"book.src must be a directory inside the repository\".\n- **Reject an absolute source path.** The component check requires every component to be `Normal` or `CurDir`, so `RootDir` and `Prefix` components fail it.\n- **Reject a parent-traversing source path.** `ParentDir` fails the same check, including when it appears mid-path, as in `md/../outside`.\n\nCallers apply the function in validation: `inspect_repository_with_progress` passes its error list to `book_source_dir`. `load_definitions` also calls it and carries its own {impl} reference. The `md` fallback after an error only lets later checks keep running, and the error is still reported.\n\nTests: `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` (src/evidence.rs 2218–2270) carries the {test} reference and covers every case above:\n- Defaults: empty file, `[book]` without `src`, and explicit `src`.\n- Inline `book = { src = … }`.\n- Missing file.\n- Invalid TOML.\n- Non-table `book`.\n- Non-string `src`: integer, boolean, array, and table.\n- Empty, absolute (`/outside`), `../outside`, and `md/../outside` paths.\n\n`configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks` also exercises the malformed-configuration report through `validate_repository`.\n\nI found no unspecified extra behavior. The \"must be a table\" and \"must be a string\" messages fall within \"malformed book configuration\". The other `book.toml` readers I found are in setup code under other requirements (`setup_project`) and in mdBook's own config loading, so they are not validation paths.",
  "references": "594482d3f97a8328232f07ec05bb4aaa35afa846b4d97168d58e53ace390245f",
